      "feature_category": "Graphics, CoreAnimation, Color, HDR & IOSurface",
      "functionality": "Manages CoreAnimation compositing layers (`CALayerHost`, `CABackdropLayer`, `CAFilter`), display links, and cross-process `CAContext` hosting.",
      "availability_3p": "apple-only-entitlement-or-daemon",
      "is_apple_only": true,
      "availability_3p_summary": "QuartzCore (CoreAnimation) in WebKit uses specialized private hosting mechanisms (CALayerHost, CAContext) and cross-process endpoint rendering. WebKit requires private entitlements to establish secure endpoints and communicate directly with CARenderServer, which are strictly denied to standard 3P apps. 3P EU browser engines rely on BrowserEngineKit's rendering hosting views (BEResponsiveLayer, BELayerHierarchyHostingView) rather than direct CARenderServer mach lookup.",
