      "availability_3p": "3p-via-browserenginekit-or-system-webkit",
      "is_apple_only": false,
      "availability_3p_summary": "UIKit contains private classes and SPIs used heavily by WebKit for custom text interaction, software keyboard interaction, input accessory views, document context, and gesture coordination (e.g. UIWKDocumentContext, BEKeyEntry, UITextSuggestion, UIKeyboardImpl). In iOS 17.4+, Apple introduced BrowserEngineKit (specifically BETextInput, BEKeyEntry, BETextAlternatives) to vend public/entitled equivalents to approved 3P browser engines with the com.apple.developer.web-browser-engine.webcontent entitlement, while raw UIKit SPI symbols remain prohibited in App Store review.",
