      "framework": "libSystem / dyld / xpc",
      "feature_category": "Process Management, RunningBoard, XPC & System Lifecycle",
      "functionality": "Uses low-level `libSystem`, `dyld`, and `libxpc` SPIs for shared-cache UUID inspection, XPC entitlement/audit-token checks, and memory warning simulation.",
      "availability_3p": "apple-only-entitlement-or-daemon",
      "is_apple_only": true,
      "availability_3p_summary": "libSystem, dyld, and libxpc provide the fundamental POSIX/Mach runtime. WebKit relies on private XPC endpoints (com.apple.private.webkit.use-xpc-endpoint), JIT dynamic code generation entitlements, extended virtual addressing, and verified JIT. 3P apps cannot hold private XPC or verified-jit entitlements, but 3P browser engines can hold com.apple.developer.cs.allow-jit and com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing under the EU browser engine entitlement.",
